title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/es/events/elections_1933.jpg
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of the Republic.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> cannot govern by itself. [? if in_republican_socialist: Since April 1931, our governments have rested on the Republican-Socialist coalition with Azaña's <span style="color: #7B2D8E;">**Republican Left**</span> and Lerroux's <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radical Party</span>. ?][? if in_radical_ceda: Since 1933, government has passed to the <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radicals</span> and the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CEDA**</span>, and we sit in opposition. ?][? if in_popular_front: Since February 1936, we govern again as part of the Popular Front, alongside the <span style="color: #7B2D8E;">**Republican Left**</span> and the <span style="color: #8a0303;">**PCE**</span>. ?] We can build ties with the other parties of the Republic, or perhaps stand alone for now.

- @izq_rep: Strengthen our bonds with Azaña's <span style="color: #7B2D8E;">**Republican Left**</span>.
- @radical: Reach out to Lerroux's <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radical Party</span>.
- @ceda: Attempt dialogue with Gil-Robles and the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CEDA**</span>.
- @pce: Work towards repairing relations with the <span style="color: #8a0303;">**PCE**</span>.
- @monarchist: Keep watch on the monarchist right.
- @falange: Establish contact with the <span style="color: #14322a;">Falange</span>.
- @psoe_alone: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@izq_rep
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: izq_rep_coalition if in_republican_socialist; izq_rep_popular_front if in_popular_front; izq_rep_op if not in_republican_socialist and not in_popular_front

@izq_rep_coalition
on-arrival: izq_rep_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); reformist_dissent -= 3

Governing together in the Republican-Socialist coalition, improving relations with the <span style="color: #7B2D8E;">**Republican Left**</span> comes naturally. The Prietistas, who champion this alliance, are pleased.

@izq_rep_popular_front
on-arrival: izq_rep_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); reformist_dissent -= 3; left_dissent -= 2

As partners in the Popular Front, our ties with Azaña's party are as close as they have ever been.

@izq_rep_op
on-arrival: izq_rep_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

Though we do not currently share government, the <span style="color: #7B2D8E;">**Republican Left**</span> remains our most natural ally in the defense of the Republic.

@radical
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: radical_coalition if in_republican_socialist; radical_ceda_era if in_radical_ceda; radical_op if not in_republican_socialist and not in_radical_ceda

@radical_coalition
on-arrival: radical_relation += 6*(1 - dissent)

As uneasy partners in the same governing coalition, cooperating with Lerroux's <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radicals</span> requires patience, but is not impossible.

@radical_ceda_era
on-arrival: radical_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); left_dissent += 3

Now governing with the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CEDA**</span>, the <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radicals</span> are wary of our overtures, and even raising the subject draws grumbling from the Caballerista left.

@radical_op
on-arrival: radical_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radical Party</span>'s political weathervane could point in many directions; it is worth keeping the door open.

@ceda
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; left_dissent += 8
go-to: ceda_gov if in_radical_ceda; ceda_op if not in_radical_ceda

@ceda_gov
on-arrival: ceda_relation += 5*(1 - dissent); reformist_dissent += 3

With the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CEDA**</span> now in government, any overture is treated with suspicion on both sides, and even raising the subject unsettles our own reformists.

@ceda_op
on-arrival: ceda_relation += 4*(1 - dissent)

Gil-Robles and the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CEDA**</span> regard us as class enemies; building even minimal goodwill is slow going.

@pce
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: pce_alliance if in_workers_alliance or in_popular_front; pce_sectarian if not in_workers_alliance and not in_popular_front

@pce_sectarian
on-arrival: pce_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); reformist_dissent += 2

The <span style="color: #8a0303;">**PCE**</span> leadership, following the Comintern's "class against class" line, dismisses us as reformists propping up bourgeois rule and brands us "social fascists." Still, some contact is made at the grassroots and local level.

@pce_alliance
on-arrival: pce_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if communist_coalition == 0

As partners in the common front against the right, the <span style="color: #8a0303;">**PCE**</span> is far more amenable to us than in years past.

@monarchist
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; monarchist_relation += 3*(1 - dissent); left_dissent += 5

Formal contact with the monarchist right — Renovación Española and the Carlists — is mostly of use for keeping an eye on their intentions. Few in the party see any real common ground, and the left is uneasy that we are talking to them at all.

@falange
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; falange_relation += 2*(1 - dissent); left_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5

There is little to be gained from reaching out to Primo de Rivera's <span style="color: #14322a;">Falange</span> — a small but violent movement with no interest in parliamentary politics. The attempt itself scandalizes much of the party.

@psoe_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
